tomli
-----
File:     .claude-plugin/scripts/_vendor/tomli/
Upstream: https://github.com/hukkin/tomli
Version:  2.4.1 (PyPI tomli-2.4.1; git tag 2.4.1)
Licence:  MIT

The `tomli` pure-Python TOML parser, vendored as a byte-faithful copy of
the upstream 2.4.1 distribution (`__init__.py`, `_parser.py`, `_re.py`,
`_types.py`, `py.typed`) together with its `LICENSE`. Pure Python with
zero dependencies.

Vendored for the same reason as `typing_extensions` above: `tomllib` is
stdlib only from Python 3.11, while this bundle's supported runtime
starts at 3.10 (requires-python >= 3.10.16, and
`scripts/bin/_bootstrap.py` states 3.10+). `tomli` IS the upstream of
stdlib `tomllib`, so the vendored parser and a 3.11+ stdlib parse agree
by construction. `commands/_dispatcher_toml_read` reads the committed
Fabro run config's checkpoint budget through it, where recognizing one
declaration across TOML's many equivalent spellings decides how much
credential lifetime a dispatch is graded against.

MIT is an OSI-approved permissive licence; its full text accompanies the
vendored copy (its `LICENSE` file).
